<div data-pf-editor-version="legacy" class="sc-jeyqhx jfeuyL __pf __pf_WyZks4vu" id="__pf"><div data-pf-type="Body" class="sc-djTQOc ejtSSi pf-8_"><div data-pf-type="Layout" class="sc-fatbYi kUsjkM pf-9_"><div data-section-id="pf-3766" data-pf-type="Section" class="sc-epRwmx cpmRjY pf-10_ pf-bg-lazy"><div style="--cw:1170px" class="sc-djVWQC dKziBg"><div class="sc-tafSX ePbmtR pf-11_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:12;--c-md:12;--c-lg:12"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-pKreJ bIaXH pf-12_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-13_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-15_">IMPACT INFO</span></p><h2 data-pf-type="Heading" class="sc-kOHUsU fHbtje pf-16_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-18_">Frequently Asked Questions</span></h2></div></div></div></div></div><div data-section-id="pf-1fd1" data-pf-type="Section" class="sc-epRwmx cpmRjY pf-19_"><div style="--cw:1170px" class="sc-djVWQC dKziBg"><div class="sc-tafSX ePbmtR pf-20_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:12;--c-md:12;--c-lg:12"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-pKreJ bIaXH pf-21_"><div class="sc-dhKdPU dlDDkz pf-22_ pf-icon-left" data-scrolling="false" data-multiple="true" data-pf-type="Accordion"><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-23_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-24_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="47e077d2-20ca-46f7-8e4e-d0620622f065" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>What features does an Impact Canopy have that makes it stand out from other available brands?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="47e077d2-20ca-46f7-8e4e-d0620622f065" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-26_"><ul style="--text-indent:0;--line-spacing:10px" data-pf-type="List" class="sc-gFmZvT iwxMkV pf-27_"><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-28_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-30_">All Impact tops are Fire Resistant rated. This in not necessarily true for many of the other competitors.</span></li><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-31_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-33_">Powder coated frame components are textured to resist scratching and finished in a bi-colour scheme to hide soiling.</span></li><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-34_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-36_">Impact frames are stronger with fewer pieces, adding to ease of use and uncomplicated maintenance.</span></li><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-37_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-39_">Impact pioneered the use of pull pins as a safer alternative to finger pinching push buttons.</span></li><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-40_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-42_">Our height-adjustable peak pole allows users to tighten up their tops to ensure a perfect fit.</span></li><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-43_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-45_">Our use of extruded, rather than seam-welded, rolled steel in the truss bars allows for stronger frames that weigh less than conventional designs.<br></span></li><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-46_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-48_">All components can be easily replaced with a commonly available Allen key.</span></li><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-49_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-51_">All canopies are provided with a tie down kit and rings at the canopy corners for securing the canopy in windy conditions.</span></li></ul></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-52_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-53_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="20ca96f7-ce4e-4062-8622-f06566a4001a" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>What sizes of frames are available?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="20ca96f7-ce4e-4062-8622-f06566a4001a" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-55_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-56_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-58_">Frame sizes may vary within the different types of frames available, but the standard sizes are:<br></span></p><ul style="--text-indent:0;--line-spacing:10px" data-pf-type="List" class="sc-gFmZvT iwxMkV pf-59_"><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-60_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-62_">5′ x 5′<br></span></li><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-63_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-65_">8′ x 8′<br></span></li><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-66_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-68_">10′ x 10′<br></span></li><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-69_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-71_">10′ x 15′<br></span></li><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-72_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-74_">10′ x 20′<br></span></li><li data-pf-type="List.Item" class="sc-dISoPS iYNNtr pf-75_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-77_">20' x 20'</span></li></ul></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-78_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-79_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="20d930be-6d6d-490d-b9f7-7c988497fd5e" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>What are Impact frames made of?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="20d930be-6d6d-490d-b9f7-7c988497fd5e" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-80_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-81_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-83_"><strong>M-Series:</strong> Super Duty aluminum | <strong>ML-Series:</strong> Commercial grade aluminum | <strong>CL-Series:</strong> Heavy Duty Steel | <strong>DS-Series:</strong> Industrial grade steel<br>CL-Series and DS-Series frames have a powder coated Hammertone textured finish.&nbsp;</span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-84_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-85_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="8497fd5e-add6-4813-a0ec-63adec93303e" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>How heavy are Impact Canopies?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="8497fd5e-add6-4813-a0ec-63adec93303e" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-86_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-87_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-89_"><strong>M-Series</strong>&nbsp;61-99 lbs | <strong>ML-Series </strong>46-73 lbs&nbsp;|&nbsp;<strong>DS-Series</strong>&nbsp;52-58 lbs |&nbsp;<strong>CL-Series</strong>&nbsp;71-122 lbs<br>* These numbers include the weight of the canopy top (~ 10-15 lbs) *</span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-90_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-91_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="ec93303e-7aae-4f48-916f-f64f71e20483" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>What are Impact tops and walls made of and are they water & fire resistant?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="ec93303e-7aae-4f48-916f-f64f71e20483" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-92_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-93_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-95_">Depending on budget and needs of the customer. We offer different material options for our tops.<br>-By defualt, Impact tops are made with heavy duty 500 denier reinforced polyester fabric, which is <strong>water resistant, fire retardant, &amp; UV treated.</strong>&nbsp;<br>- For light use and budget applications we offer 300 denier and 600 denier options upon customer request.<br><br></span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-96_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-97_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="71e20483-683e-4060-867e-f950569de0cc" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>Can Impact Canopy tops be washed?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="71e20483-683e-4060-867e-f950569de0cc" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-98_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-99_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-101_">By using a mild detergent and a soft brush, you can rinse down your Impact Canopy with a garden hose. Ensure your top is completely dry before you fold and store it. This being said, you should avoid rigorous scrubbing of your canopy top if you have graphics on it.</span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-102_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-103_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="569de0cc-c2df-46a5-bb4b-fb1b7668ae73" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>Can Impact Canopies handle wind and rain?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="569de0cc-c2df-46a5-bb4b-fb1b7668ae73" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-104_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-105_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-107_">Impact Canopies are manufactured to provide instant protection from the elements. They stand securely on dirt, grass, or pavement; To avoid damage caused by severe wind conditions, it is best that they are staked or weighted down. Our tops have optional sealant along the canopies sewing seems to prevent water leaks. Though they can withstand the elements, please be reminded that Impact Canopies are not meant to be a permanent structure, so they should not be left unattended for lengthy periods of time.</span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-108_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-109_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="7668ae73-262f-46cb-b898-f2d6c6bdcebb" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>How can I try out an Impact Canopy to see if it will meet my needs?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="7668ae73-262f-46cb-b898-f2d6c6bdcebb" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-110_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-111_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-113_">If you rent a Impact Canopy from us, and decide within 30 days of the rental that you would like to buy one, we will deduct the cost of the rental from your purchase.<br><br></span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-114_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-115_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="c6bdcebb-38bb-4473-b304-50edc720c3ed" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>What stock colors are available for the tops & commercial grade walls?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="c6bdcebb-38bb-4473-b304-50edc720c3ed" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-116_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-117_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-119_">Standard Impact colours include white, black, grey, kelly green, lime green, forest green, orange, red, burgundy, royal blue, and navy blue.<br><br></span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-120_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-121_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="c720c3ed-c964-4814-9a3c-39aad6b62163" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>I'd like to put my company logo on my canopy top. What options do I have?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="c720c3ed-c964-4814-9a3c-39aad6b62163" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-122_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-123_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-125_">You are not limited to only your logo! Our professional Graphics Department will work with you to create a canopy design that will <strong>Build </strong><strong>your Brand Instantly</strong>.<br> At Impact Canopy we offer all solutions for high quaility printing needs:<br>Our full digital dye sublimation printing process allows customers to&nbsp;include any color and design they require.&nbsp;<br></span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-126_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-127_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="d6b62163-16fd-45e7-94c9-6bc26a5d1f2f" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>What do I need to provide for a custom canopy?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="d6b62163-16fd-45e7-94c9-6bc26a5d1f2f" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-128_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-129_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-131_">For proper resigning capabilies: vector artwork is best (.svg .ai .esp) | To uphold your branding standards: pantone colors are necessary&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>We will work with what you can provide. Our in house design team has the capability of turning lower quality artwork into vector logos that will keep your logo looking sharp when its time for printing.&nbsp;</span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-132_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-133_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="6a5d1f2f-0c57-4017-8eb6-bc617b9be866" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>Are they really that quick to set up?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="6a5d1f2f-0c57-4017-8eb6-bc617b9be866" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-134_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-135_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-137_">Yes, they set up quickly, easily and with no tools needed. With our truss design, you can open and close your canopy all by yourself in a matter of minutes. By leaving the top on, there aren’t any loose parts. You’ll love it!</span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-138_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-139_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="7b9be866-6407-4876-ac18-ba06c7f34f90" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>What kind of warranty does an Impact have?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="7b9be866-6407-4876-ac18-ba06c7f34f90" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-140_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-141_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-143_">Impact Canopy offers different warranties based on the product you purchased. Please see our “warranty” section of the website.<br><br></span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-144_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-145_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="c7f34f90-09ba-40a7-8018-ca7e48e368ba" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>How long can I expect my canopy to last?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="c7f34f90-09ba-40a7-8018-ca7e48e368ba" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-146_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-147_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-149_"><strong>The lifespan of an Impact Canopy ranges from 3 to 8 years,</strong> depending on how often it's used, the conditions it's exposed to, and how it's stored. Frequent daily use will shorten its life, while occasional use can extend it.The frame can last indefinitely with care, though tops may need replacement due to rebranding, promotions, or damage.We back every canopy with a 2-year warranty—twice as long as our nearest competitor—because we believe in the quality of our products.</span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-150_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-151_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="48e368ba-b9e7-45f3-853b-b908c707df54" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>Who do I contact if I need replacement parts or tops?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="48e368ba-b9e7-45f3-853b-b908c707df54" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-152_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-153_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-155_">Replacement parts and stock fabric and be purchased through our website.&nbsp;For additional support and replacement needs<br>Call on our toll-free number (877) 840-3524 or emails us at myquote@impactcanopy.com&nbsp;<br>* We will get back to you in under 24 hours *</span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-156_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-157_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="c707df54-e754-43d3-9e95-8a831e2bf53c" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>What tools do I need if replacing a part?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="c707df54-e754-43d3-9e95-8a831e2bf53c" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-158_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-159_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-161_">A Philips screwdriver or allen key is all you need.</span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-162_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-163_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="1e2bf53c-bce0-4efd-9ae9-6f61c2625b81" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>What is the height of an Impact Canopy?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="1e2bf53c-bce0-4efd-9ae9-6f61c2625b81" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-164_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-165_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-167_">Depending on what height you chose to have your Impact set up at, all our models range from a minimum of 10’3 to a maximum of 11’6″<br>To check the setup height for your particular frame, visit the spec sheet section of our website.&nbsp;</span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-168_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-169_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="c2625b81-b6ca-42bf-a6c6-3fdf40343d08" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>What is the clearance on an Impact Canopy?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="c2625b81-b6ca-42bf-a6c6-3fdf40343d08" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-170_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-171_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-173_">The total clearance of a Impact is the Industry’s best! From the ground to the lowest truss, all of our models have a clearance from a minimum of 5′ 10″ to a maximum of 7’1″</span></p></div></div><div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-kpDprT ifeEKM pf-174_"><button type="button" class="sc-imWZod yQSGW pf-175_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor" data-header-id="40343d08-0140-458c-9b8f-350d2318f30b" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow"></i><span>What other Impact products do you have?</span></button><div data-pf-expandable="true" data-id="40343d08-0140-458c-9b8f-350d2318f30b" style="display:none" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-jXbVAB fMPMgo pf-176_"><p class="sc-feopBa gVincu pf-177_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-cRmpXP cGRimR pf-179_">Impact produces&nbsp;wide variety of custom and nonbranded&nbsp;products, &nbsp;These include flags,&nbsp;banners, table covers, display signs, inflatables, chairs, wagons, and umbrellas. Not to mention a wide selection of accessories like dust covers, wheeled bags, deluxe bags, weight bags, mesh walls plus more…&nbsp;</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><script>
